---
// Commercial terms: a plain summary of MedBrains' standard terms. The signed order form and
// agreement prevail. Owner: the founder.
//
// TO CONFIRM (founder / lawyer), kept off the page until decided:
// - Refunds: implementation fees for work done are non-refundable; unused prepaid AMC is refunded
//   pro rata only if MedBrains ends the AMC without cause. Confirm before it binds anyone.
// - Jurisdiction: courts of which city. The page says only "governed by the laws of India".
// - Limitation of liability: the cap (e.g. fees paid in the previous 12 months) belongs in the
//   agreement; the page only points to it.
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import WhatsAppFloat from "../components/WhatsAppFloat.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "25 October 2026";
const home = new URL("/", Astro.site).href;
const url = new URL("/terms", Astro.site).href;
const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: SITE.brand, item: home },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Commercial terms", item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={`Commercial terms | ${SITE.brand}`}
  description="MedBrains commercial terms in plain words: free software and updates, paid implementation, customisation and AMC, payment, hosting, data and exit."
  schema={schema}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="policy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs-dark" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">{SITE.brand}</a> / <span>Commercial terms</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial terms</p>
      <h1>Our commercial terms</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This page summarises our standard terms in plain words. Your signed order
        form and agreement prevail over anything here. See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for
        what is free and what we charge for.
      </p>

      <h2>What is free</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The MedBrains software licence, for every hospital and clinic.</li>
        <li>Every update: new versions and features, for as long as you run MedBrains.</li>
        <li>There is no subscription and no charge per user.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we charge for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Implementation.</strong> A one-time service to set MedBrains up for your
          hospital: configuration of departments, tariffs, forms and masters, data
          migration, staff training and go-live support. The scope is written in your quote.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Customisation.</strong> Reports, forms, integrations or features specific
          to your hospital, scoped and quoted per requirement before any work starts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Annual Maintenance Contract (AMC).</strong> Support, bug fixes,
          monitoring, backups, help desk and small configuration changes, and hosting in
          AWS Mumbai if we host MedBrains for you. An AMC runs for 12 months and renews yearly
          by agreement. Support hours and response times are as set out in your AMC.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        SMS, WhatsApp and heavy use of a hosted AI model are passed through at the
        provider's cost, with no mark-up.
      </p>

      <h2>Pilot period</h2>
      <p>
        Before any contract, a hospital may run a pilot of MedBrains for one month after
        the free assessment. The pilot is free of charge. Its scope, such as the
        departments and modules included and whether we host it, is agreed in writing
        before it starts. There is no obligation to continue. At the end of the pilot, if
        you go ahead, your pilot data carries over into your implementation; if you do
        not, we export your data to you and delete our copies on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Quotes and payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Quotes are valid for 30 days from the date on them.</li>
        <li>Implementation and customisation are invoiced in stages, as stated in your quote or order form.</li>
        <li>AMC is invoiced yearly in advance.</li>
        <li>GST is added at the applicable rate.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where MedBrains runs</h2>
      <p>
        You choose: on your own server, or hosted by us in Amazon Web Services Mumbai
        (ap-south-1). When we host, hosting is part of your AMC.
      </p>

      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your hospital owns its data, including every patient record.</li>
        <li>We export your data on request, in standard formats.</li>
        <li>When you leave, we return your data and then delete our copies, as agreed with you.</li>
        <li>
          For patient data we act as a data processor under the Digital Personal Data
          Protection Act, 2023: we process it only on your instructions, under a data
          processing agreement, and keep it confidential.
        </li>
        <li>How we handle personal data from this website and your enquiries is in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our promises</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No money from pharmaceutical companies or advertisers reaches the product.</li>
        <li>We never sell clinical data.</li>
        <li>Every patient-safety feature is free for everyone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If an AMC lapses</h2>
      <p>
        The software keeps working and updates stay free. Support, monitoring and
        hosting stop. If we host MedBrains for you, we give 30 days' notice and a full
        export of your data before hosting stops.
      </p>

      <h2>Ending the agreement</h2>
      <p>
        Fees for implementation and customisation work already done are not refundable.
        Refunds of prepaid AMC are as set out in your agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Supporting MedBrains</h2>
      <p>
        Organisations may choose to support MedBrains' development: by lending their IT
        team to test releases, contributing development or ideas, sponsoring a feature or
        making a voluntary yearly contribution. It is optional and does not change your
        support. Any payment is invoiced to MedBrains with GST as applicable; it is not a
        donation. Code or ideas you contribute are covered by a short written agreement
        before work starts. We accept no sponsorship from pharmaceutical
        companies or advertisers. See <a href="/sponsors">ways to sponsor MedBrains</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability and law</h2>
      <p>
        Limits on liability are as set out in your agreement. These terms are governed by
        the laws of India.
      </p>

      <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <WhatsAppFloat />
</Base>

<style>
  .policy { padding: 72px 0 96px; }
  .policy .wrap { max-width: 760px; }
  .crumbs-dark { margin-bottom: 28px; font-size: .88rem; color: var(--night-text); }
  .crumbs-dark a { color: #fff; }
  .policy h1 { margin: 8px 0 4px; }
  .policy h2 { margin: 40px 0 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .policy .meta { color: var(--night-text); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .policy p, .policy li { line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy ul { padding-left: 1.2em; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
</style>
